    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0890" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2491/50–52.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Squiers to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-01-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 1, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 410.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to department’s instructions
                    (file No. 2491/40) serial No. 137, December 1, last, respecting the Costa Rica
                    boundary dispute, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of my note of
                    December 21, last, to the minister for foreign affairs, and his reply of
                    December 26, with translation.</p>
                <p>I have received department’s last instructions of December 16, last,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d849-f1"/> and departments cable of December 31, the latter of which
                    I shall immediately bring to the notice of the Panaman Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d849-a1.xml" xpointer="d849-a1"/>
